// gino plugin contract, v1.
//
// A plugin is a binary gino starts in its own pod and talks to over a unix socket (path in the
// GINO_PLUGIN_SOCKET env var). Every collector is a plugin, gino's own included: the runtime owns
// the assignment, the schedule, publishing and retry pacing, the plugin owns sessions and how to
// talk to devices. A pipeline chooses a plugin by choosing a worker image.
//
// Errors ride on gRPC status, not on message fields:
//   OK                                        collected / transformed
//   INVALID_ARGUMENT, FAILED_PRECONDITION,
//   INTERNAL                                  this request failed; gino backs off this input
//                                             (collector) or sends the message to the fail
//                                             stream (transformer) and carries on
//   UNAVAILABLE (Collect)                     the endpoint's session is lost; gino Opens again
//                                             before the next Collect for that endpoint
//   transport error, or Ping failing          the plugin is dead; gino restarts it
//
// Logs: write JSON lines to stderr ({"level":..,"msg":..,...}); gino re-emits them through its
// own logger tagged with the plugin's name. Nothing on stdout is read.
//
// Data vs protocol: proto carries the protocol (services, payloads, timestamps, fn chains). Gino's
// own data -- the endpoint, an input's implementation -- crosses as JSON bytes of the sdk's Go
// types (apis/v1), so there is one schema for the CRD, the message bus and the plugin boundary.
// Go plugins unmarshal into those types; others read the CRD's documented shape.

